WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.060 --> 00:00:05.040
How did the villain in Wakanda Forever&nbsp;
steal the show? And what was the biggest&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:05.040 --> 00:00:08.220
complaint about the movie? Keep&nbsp;
watching for what critics are&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:08.220 --> 00:00:11.400
saying about the latest installment&nbsp;
in the Marvel Cinematic Universe.

00:00:12.060 --> 00:00:16.620
Going into this film, many MCU fans&nbsp;
were wondering how it would handle&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:16.620 --> 00:00:19.860
the death of Chadwick Boseman.&nbsp;
We can't give anything away,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:19.860 --> 00:00:25.800
but Twitter reactions are proving Ryan Coogler&nbsp;
honored his friend properly. One critic tweeted,

00:00:43.320 --> 00:00:44.940
Another agreed, adding,

00:00:56.280 --> 00:01:00.780
A major theme being discussed on Twitter&nbsp;
is the world-building Coogler managed&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:00.780 --> 00:01:04.920
to cram in the film's two-hour and&nbsp;
41-minute runtime. Wakanda Forever&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:04.920 --> 00:01:08.880
introduces the underwater nation&nbsp;
of Talokan, where Namor reigns.

00:01:08.880 --> 00:01:14.520
It certainly is not easy to introduce a whole&nbsp;
new world in the MCU, especially within a movie&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:14.520 --> 00:01:19.200
focused on Wakanda and its people. One&nbsp;
critic wrote that Wakanda Forever is a,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:19.200 --> 00:01:25.320
quote, "solid mix of developing [a] post-Chadwick&nbsp;
path, plus world-building for future MCU stories."

00:01:25.320 --> 00:01:28.200
Wakanda Forever is certainly an emotional outing,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:28.200 --> 00:01:33.360
but Twitter reviews suggest it's so much more&nbsp;
than a legacy film. It's also a throwback to&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:33.360 --> 00:01:37.117
the great films of The Infinity Saga,&nbsp;
including the original Black Panther.

00:01:37.117 --> 00:01:37.140
"Show them who we are."

00:01:37.140 --> 00:01:42.900
Finding a Wakanda Forever tweet that doesn't&nbsp;
praise Angela Bassett is like finding a needle&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:42.900 --> 00:01:47.940
in a haystack. The Academy Award nominee,&nbsp;
who played Queen Ramonda might get another&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:47.940 --> 00:01:53.220
nod thrown her way at the next Oscars if Twitter&nbsp;
has anything to say about it. One critic tweeted,

00:02:07.320 --> 00:02:10.310
"Have I not given everything?"

00:02:10.310 --> 00:02:13.800
Another shining star in Wakanda&nbsp;
Forever is Tenoch Huerta,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:13.800 --> 00:02:17.640
who is getting ample amounts of praise&nbsp;
on social media. A critic wrote,

00:02:19.740 --> 00:02:20.940
Another added,

00:02:26.040 --> 00:02:30.240
Wright also gets lots of compliments on&nbsp;
Twitter, with a film YouTuber writing,

00:02:37.860 --> 00:02:41.280
If the tweets surrounding Wakanda&nbsp;
Forever are any indication,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:41.280 --> 00:02:46.860
this might just be the best film in Phase 4&nbsp;
of the MCU. It will likely battle Spider-Man:&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:46.860 --> 00:02:52.020
No Way Home in debates about the best, but if&nbsp;
you're looking for a solid, well-rounded film&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:52.020 --> 00:02:56.760
that doesn't rely on fanfare and cameos, the&nbsp;
Black Panther sequel looks to take the cake.

00:02:57.360 --> 00:03:01.080
Perhaps one of the biggest talking&nbsp;
points amongst moviegoers is Namor,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:01.080 --> 00:03:06.600
as the MCU's newest villain is a scene-stealer.&nbsp;
After seeing the flick Thursday, a viewer wrote,

00:03:21.718 --> 00:03:24.841
"He's coming for the surface world."

00:03:24.841 --> 00:03:26.485
Someone else agreed, writing,

00:03:32.700 --> 00:03:34.560
"But my enemies call me Namor."

00:03:34.560 --> 00:03:39.360
The MCU has always had something of a&nbsp;
villain problem. Sure, there are some greats,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:39.360 --> 00:03:44.700
but a majority of the Marvel antagonists have&nbsp;
been either relatively dull or total duds that&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:44.700 --> 00:03:49.860
lack the complexity of the movies' good guys. It&nbsp;
looks like Namor is helping to balance it all out,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:49.860 --> 00:03:54.480
as the character is being hailed as one of&nbsp;
the film's highlights. Another viewer tweeted,

00:04:00.900 --> 00:04:05.040
If you scan the Wakanda Forever tweets,&nbsp;
you'll notice one theme more than any&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:05.040 --> 00:04:09.180
other — the movie perfectly honors&nbsp;
Chadwick Boseman. There are hundreds&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:09.180 --> 00:04:12.780
upon hundreds of tweets mentioning the&nbsp;
late actor and how the film pays its&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:12.780 --> 00:04:17.160
respects to him. One person said they became&nbsp;
emotional during their screening, writing,

00:04:21.600 --> 00:04:24.780
Someone else agreed, tweeting,

00:04:33.360 --> 00:04:37.260
Like we said earlier, don't forget&nbsp;
those tissues before sitting down for&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:37.260 --> 00:04:41.940
Wakanda Forever. Many tweets indicate the&nbsp;
film is a tear-jerker, with one reading,

00:04:50.110 --> 00:04:55.980
"We had been kinda, in a way, we had been keeping him alive by working on the film."

00:04:55.980 --> 00:04:59.640
Of course, there were criticisms.&nbsp;
You can't please everyone these days,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:59.640 --> 00:05:04.920
especially movie fans. While it's difficult to&nbsp;
find a tweet that totally bashes Wakanda Forever,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:05:04.920 --> 00:05:08.700
there are plenty that point out&nbsp;
its flaws, with one viewer writing,

00:05:18.540 --> 00:05:22.380
When it comes to the not-so-glowing&nbsp;
comments about the movie, it looks&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:05:22.380 --> 00:05:28.260
like a lot of moviegoers thought the 161-minute&nbsp;
runtime was just too much. Someone else wrote,

00:05:38.520 --> 00:05:40.620
Another viewer agreed, adding,

00:05:46.080 --> 00:05:48.780
If the biggest complaint people have about Wakanda&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:05:48.780 --> 00:05:52.620
Forever is that it's a little bit too&nbsp;
long, we'd say it's still a winner. 
 
 

